IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 168 -- payments to a director for loss of office -- and s 169 -- provision and improvement of a director's emoluments.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part sgb2. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
--
-- HOW IT READS. s 168(1): it is not lawful to pay a director compensation for loss of office or retirement, or to pay a director in connection with a transfer of the company's undertaking or property,
-- unless the particulars (including the amount) have been disclosed to the members and the proposal approved in general meeting. (1A) lifts the approval for a payment to a salaried director under an existing
-- legal obligation up to the last year's emoluments, if disclosed upon or before the payment. (5) lists payments the section's references to compensation do not include. s 169: no provision or improvement of a
-- director's emoluments unless approved by a resolution not related to other matters. Whether a corporation is "related" by s 6 is a fact here (the seat builds it from the keel's s 6 function).

§ `Section 168(1): payments that are not lawful without disclosure and approval`

DECLARE `s 168(1) kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `s 168(1)(a) a payment by way of compensation for loss of office, or as consideration for or in connection with retirement from office`
    `s 168(1)(b) a payment in connection with the transfer of the whole or any part of the undertaking or property of the company`
    `s 168(1) some other payment`

DECLARE `s 168 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 168(1)(a) make the payment by way of compensation for loss of office or as consideration for retirement`
    `s 168(2) take all reasonable steps to secure that the particulars are included in or sent with the notice of the offer`

-- (1): "It is not lawful (a) ... or (b) ..., unless particulars with respect to the proposed payment, including the amount thereof, have been disclosed to the members of the company and the proposal has been
-- approved by the company in general meeting". The approval is not needed where (1A) applies. "Director" is read with subsection (7).
-- src:14405 | 168.—(1) It is not lawful —
-- src:14407 | (a) for a company to make to any director any payment by way
-- src:14408 | of compensation for loss of office as an officer of the
-- src:14409 | company or of a subsidiary of the company or as
-- src:14410 | consideration for or in connection with his or her
-- src:14411 | retirement from any such office; or
-- src:14413 | (b) for any payment to be made to any director of a company in
-- src:14414 | connection with the transfer of the whole or any part of the
-- src:14415 | undertaking or property of the company,
-- src:14417 | unless particulars with respect to the proposed payment, including the
-- src:14418 | amount thereof, have been disclosed to the members of the company
-- src:14419 | and the proposal has been approved by the company in general
-- src:14420 | meeting and when any such payment has been unlawfully made the
@ref s 168(1) (src:14405-14420)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 168(1) kind of payment`
      `the payee is a director, or by subsection (7) has at any time been a director of the company or of a corporation deemed by section 6 to be related to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is one that the references in the section to compensation for loss of office do not include, by subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement for approval does not apply to the payment by subsection (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `particulars with respect to the proposed payment, including the amount, have been disclosed to the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal has been approved by the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(1) the payment is unlawful` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the payee is a director, or by subsection (7) has at any time been a director of the company or of a corporation deemed by section 6 to be related to it`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is not lawful (a) for a company to make to any director any payment ... (b) for any payment to be made to any director" limits the bar to payments to a director, with no "only"
    ELSE CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `s 168(1) some other payment` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names two kinds of payment and says nothing of any other
         OTHERWISE
             (IF kind EQUALS `s 168(1)(a) a payment by way of compensation for loss of office, or as consideration for or in connection with retirement from office` AND `the payment is one that the references in the section to compensation for loss of office do not include, by subsection (5)`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any reference in this section to payments ... by way of compensation for loss of office ... does not include" the payments (5)(a) to (e) lists (a flat negative: N2 of 2026-11-04)
              ELSE IF `particulars with respect to the proposed payment, including the amount, have been disclosed to the members of the company` AND (`the proposal has been approved by the company in general meeting` OR `the requirement for approval does not apply to the payment by subsection (1A)`)
                   THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless particulars ... have been disclosed to the members of the company and the proposal has been approved by the company in general meeting" (an "unless" once met; fork F-168-1 in NOTES.md)
                   ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- The bearer of the prohibition in (a) is the company. In (b) "any payment to be made to any director of a company in connection with the transfer" names no payer, so no rule is derived for (b)
-- (N2 of 2026-11-04: "where the text names the bearer the prohibition (`SHANT`) is derived from that answer"; fork F-168-1).
-- src:14407 | (a) for a company to make to any director any payment by way
-- src:14408 | of compensation for loss of office as an officer of the
-- src:14409 | company or of a subsidiary of the company or as
-- src:14410 | consideration for or in connection with his or her
-- src:14411 | retirement from any such office; or
@ref s 168(1)(a) (src:14407-14411)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `particulars with respect to the proposed payment, including the amount, have been disclosed to the members of the company and the proposal has been approved by the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 168 act`
`s 168(1)(a) the company must not make to a director a payment by way of compensation for loss of office without disclosure to the members and approval in general meeting` MEANS
    IF `particulars with respect to the proposed payment, including the amount, have been disclosed to the members of the company and the proposal has been approved by the company in general meeting`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY Company `the name of the company`
         SHANT `s 168(1)(a) make the payment by way of compensation for loss of office or as consideration for retirement`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company made to a director a payment by way of compensation for loss of office or as consideration for retirement without disclosing the particulars to the members and obtaining the approval of the company in general meeting"

-- (1), closing words: "when any such payment has been unlawfully made the amount received by the director is deemed to have been received by him or her in trust for the company". "When" counts as "where" (the delegated
-- ruling (c) of 2026-11-05), so a payment not unlawfully made gives JUST FALSE (fork F-168-3).
-- src:14420 | meeting and when any such payment has been unlawfully made the
-- src:14421 | amount received by the director is deemed to have been received by
-- src:14422 | him or her in trust for the company.
@ref s 168(1) (src:14420-14422)
GIVEN `the payment has been unlawfully made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(1) the amount received by the director is deemed to have been received in trust for the company` MEANS
    IF `the payment has been unlawfully made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when any such payment has been unlawfully made the amount received by the director is deemed to have been received by him or her in trust for the company" ("when" counts as "where": the delegated ruling (c) of 2026-11-05, and the periods ruling (b): a failed "where" gives JUST FALSE)

§ `Section 168(1A) and (1B): the approval is not needed for a payment under an existing legal obligation`

-- (1A)(a): "the amount of the payment does not exceed the total emoluments of the director for the year immediately preceding his or her termination of employment".
-- src:14431 | (a) the amount of the payment does not exceed the total
-- src:14432 | emoluments of the director for the year immediately
-- src:14433 | preceding his or her termination of employment; and
@ref s 168(1A)(a) (src:14431-14433)
GIVEN `the amount of the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the total emoluments of the director for the year immediately preceding the termination of employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(1A)(a) the amount of the payment does not exceed the total emoluments of the director for the preceding year` MEANS
    IF `the amount of the payment` AT MOST `the total emoluments of the director for the year immediately preceding the termination of employment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (a) the amount of the payment does not exceed the total emoluments of the director for the year immediately preceding his or her termination of employment" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))

-- (1A)(b): "the particulars with respect to the proposed payment, including the amount thereof, have been disclosed to the members of the company upon or prior to the payment".
-- src:14438 | (b) the particulars with respect to the proposed payment,
-- src:14439 | including the amount thereof, have been disclosed to the
-- src:14440 | members of the company upon or prior to the payment.
@ref s 168(1A)(b) (src:14438-14440)
GIVEN `the day the particulars were disclosed to the members of the company` IS A DATE
      `the day of the payment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(1A)(b) the particulars have been disclosed to the members upon or prior to the payment` MEANS
    IF `the day the particulars were disclosed to the members of the company` AT MOST `the day of the payment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (b) the particulars ... have been disclosed to the members of the company upon or prior to the payment" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))

-- src:14424 | (1A) The requirement for approval by the company in
-- src:14425 | subsection (1) does not apply in respect of any payment to a
-- src:14426 | director holding a salaried employment or office in the company by
-- src:14427 | way of compensation for termination of employment pursuant to an
-- src:14428 | existing legal obligation arising from an agreement made between the
-- src:14429 | company and the director if —
@ref s 168(1A) (src:14424-14429)
GIVEN `the director holds a salaried employment or office in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is by way of compensation for termination of employment pursuant to an existing legal obligation arising from an agreement made between the company and the director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the total emoluments of the director for the year immediately preceding the termination of employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the particulars were disclosed to the members of the company` IS A DATE
      `the day of the payment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(1A) the requirement for approval does not apply to the payment` MEANS
    IF    `the director holds a salaried employment or office in the company`
      AND `the payment is by way of compensation for termination of employment pursuant to an existing legal obligation arising from an agreement made between the company and the director`
      AND (`s 168(1A)(a) the amount of the payment does not exceed the total emoluments of the director for the preceding year` `the amount of the payment` `the total emoluments of the director for the year immediately preceding the termination of employment`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND (`s 168(1A)(b) the particulars have been disclosed to the members upon or prior to the payment` `the day the particulars were disclosed to the members of the company` `the day of the payment`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirement for approval by the company in subsection (1) does not apply in respect of any payment to a director holding a salaried employment or office ... if" (a) and (b) (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))

-- src:14446 | (a) an existing legal obligation is an obligation of the
-- src:14447 | company, or any corporation which is by virtue of
-- src:14448 | section 6 deemed to be related to the company, that was
-- src:14449 | not entered into in connection with, or in consequence of,
-- src:14450 | the event giving rise to the payment for loss of office; and
@ref s 168(1B)(a) (src:14446-14450)
GIVEN `the obligation is an obligation of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation is an obligation of a corporation that is by virtue of section 6 deemed to be related to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation was entered into in connection with, or in consequence of, the event giving rise to the payment for loss of office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(1B)(a) the obligation is an existing legal obligation` MEANS
    IF (`the obligation is an obligation of the company` OR `the obligation is an obligation of a corporation that is by virtue of section 6 deemed to be related to the company`) AND (NOT `the obligation was entered into in connection with, or in consequence of, the event giving rise to the payment for loss of office`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an existing legal obligation is an obligation of the company, or any corporation which is by virtue of section 6 deemed to be related to the company, that was not entered into in connection with, or in consequence of, the event giving rise to the payment" (a definition that fixes what is meant: fork F-162-12, read the same way)

-- src:14452 | (b) if paragraph (a) or (b) of that subsection is not complied
-- src:14453 | with, the amount received by the director is deemed to have
-- src:14454 | been received by him or her on trust for the company.
@ref s 168(1B)(b) (src:14452-14454)
GIVEN `the payment was made in reliance on subsection (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (a) of subsection (1A) is complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b) of subsection (1A) is complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(1B)(b) the amount received by the director is deemed to have been received on trust for the company` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the payment was made in reliance on subsection (1A)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsection (1A) ... if paragraph (a) or (b) of that subsection is not complied with" speaks only of a payment under subsection (1A)
    ELSE IF `paragraph (a) of subsection (1A) is complied with` AND `paragraph (b) of subsection (1A) is complied with`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if paragraph (a) or (b) of that subsection is not complied with, the amount received by the director is deemed to have been received by him or her on trust" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a); fork F-168-3)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 168(2) and (3): payments on a take-over offer`

-- (2): "Where such a payment is to be made to a director in connection with the transfer to any person, as a result of an offer made to shareholders, of all or any of the shares in the company, that director must
-- take all reasonable steps to secure that particulars with respect to the proposed payment, including the amount thereof, are included in or sent with any notice of the offer made for their shares which is given
-- to any shareholders, unless those particulars are furnished to the shareholders by virtue of any requirement of law relating to take-over offers or any requirement of the Take-over Code".
-- src:14458 | (2) Where such a payment is to be made to a director in connection
-- src:14459 | with the transfer to any person, as a result of an offer made to
-- src:14460 | shareholders, of all or any of the shares in the company, that director
-- src:14461 | must take all reasonable steps to secure that particulars with respect to
-- src:14462 | the proposed payment, including the amount thereof, are included in
-- src:14463 | or sent with any notice of the offer made for their shares which is
-- src:14464 | given to any shareholders, unless those particulars are furnished to
-- src:14465 | the shareholders by virtue of any requirement of law relating to
-- src:14466 | take‑over offers or any requirement of the Take‑over Code mentioned
-- src:14467 | in section 139 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001.
@ref s 168(2) (src:14458-14467)
GIVEN `a payment is to be made to the director in connection with the transfer to any person, as a result of an offer made to shareholders, of all or any of the shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those particulars are furnished to the shareholders by virtue of any requirement of law relating to take-over offers or any requirement of the Take-over Code mentioned in section 139 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(2) the director must take all reasonable steps to secure that the particulars are included in or sent with the notice of the offer` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a payment is to be made to the director in connection with the transfer to any person, as a result of an offer made to shareholders, of all or any of the shares in the company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where such a payment is to be made to a director in connection with the transfer ... that director must take all reasonable steps" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))
    ELSE IF `those particulars are furnished to the shareholders by virtue of any requirement of law relating to take-over offers or any requirement of the Take-over Code mentioned in section 139 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless those particulars are furnished to the shareholders by virtue of any requirement of law" (an "unless" once met: fork F-168-1 reading)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The duty has no period: "all reasonable steps" with no time. A "must" with no deadline can never reach BREACH, so the rule is listed under "Rules with no breach path" in NOTES.md.
