-- src:14467 | in section 139 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001.
@ref s 168(2) (src:14458-14467)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 168 act`
`s 168(2) the director must take all reasonable steps to secure that the particulars are included in or sent with the notice of the offer` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 168(2) take all reasonable steps to secure that the particulars are included in or sent with the notice of the offer`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- (3), the offence: "A director who fails to comply with subsection (2) and a person who has been properly required by a director to include in or send with any notice under this section the particulars required by that
-- subsection and who fails to do so shall be guilty of an offence". The subsection states no penalty: the general penalty of the Act (s 417, a later wave) is not read from memory; no penalty function is written.
-- src:14469 | (3) A director who fails to comply with subsection (2) and a person
