      `the person has been properly required by a director to include in or send with the notice the particulars required by subsection (2) and fails to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(3) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director who fails to comply with subsection (2)` OR `the person has been properly required by a director to include in or send with the notice the particulars required by subsection (2) and fails to do so`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A director who fails to comply with subsection (2) and a person who has been properly required ... and who fails to do so shall be guilty" names who is guilty, with no "only" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c); split site (i), fork F-168-3 in NOTES.md)

-- (3), the trust: "if the requirements of that subsection are not complied with any sum received by the director on account of the payment is deemed to have been received by him or her in trust for any person who has
-- sold the person's shares as a result of the offer made".
