-- src:14476 | person’s shares as a result of the offer made.
@ref s 168(3) (src:14472-14476)
GIVEN `the requirements of subsection (2) are not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has sold the person's shares as a result of the offer made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(3) any sum received by the director on account of the payment is deemed to have been received in trust for the person` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the requirements of subsection (2) are not complied with`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the requirements of that subsection are not complied with any sum received by the director on account of the payment is deemed to have been received by him or her in trust" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))
    ELSE IF `the person has sold the person's shares as a result of the offer made`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the trust is "for any person who has sold the person's shares as a result of the offer made", with no "only"; the subsection says nothing of any other person

§ `Section 168(4): a price above what other holders could have had`

-- (4): "If in connection with any such transfer the price to be paid to a director of the company whose office is to be abolished or who is to retire from office for any shares in the company held by him or her is in
-- excess of the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of the like shares or any valuable consideration is given to any such director, the excess or the money value of the consideration
-- (as the case may be) is for the purposes of this section deemed to have been a payment made to the director by way of compensation for loss of office".
-- src:14478 | (4) If in connection with any such transfer the price to be paid to a
-- src:14479 | director of the company whose office is to be abolished or who is to
-- src:14480 | retire from office for any shares in the company held by him or her is
-- src:14481 | in excess of the price which could at the time have been obtained by
-- src:14486 | other holders of the like shares or any valuable consideration is given
-- src:14487 | to any such director, the excess or the money value of the
-- src:14488 | consideration (as the case may be) is for the purposes of this
-- src:14489 | section deemed to have been a payment made to the director by way
-- src:14490 | of compensation for loss of office or as consideration for or in
-- src:14491 | connection with his or her retirement from office.
@ref s 168(4) (src:14478-14491)
GIVEN `the price to be paid to the director for the shares the director holds` IS A NUMBER
      `the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of the like shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 168(4) the excess of the price paid to the director over the price other holders could have obtained` MEANS
    IF `the price to be paid to the director for the shares the director holds` GREATER THAN `the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of the like shares`
    THEN `the price to be paid to the director for the shares the director holds` MINUS `the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of the like shares`
    ELSE 0

-- src:14478 | (4) If in connection with any such transfer the price to be paid to a
-- src:14479 | director of the company whose office is to be abolished or who is to
-- src:14480 | retire from office for any shares in the company held by him or her is
-- src:14481 | in excess of the price which could at the time have been obtained by
-- src:14486 | other holders of the like shares or any valuable consideration is given
-- src:14487 | to any such director, the excess or the money value of the
-- src:14488 | consideration (as the case may be) is for the purposes of this
-- src:14489 | section deemed to have been a payment made to the director by way
-- src:14490 | of compensation for loss of office or as consideration for or in
-- src:14491 | connection with his or her retirement from office.
@ref s 168(4) (src:14478-14491)
GIVEN `the transfer is one in connection with which a payment is made to a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director's office is to be abolished or the director is to retire from office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the price to be paid to the director for the shares the director holds` IS A NUMBER
      `the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of the like shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the money value of any valuable consideration given to the director` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(4) the excess or the money value of the consideration is deemed to be a payment by way of compensation for loss of office` MEANS
    IF    `the transfer is one in connection with which a payment is made to a director`
      AND `the director's office is to be abolished or the director is to retire from office`
      AND (   `the price to be paid to the director for the shares the director holds` GREATER THAN `the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of the like shares`
           OR `the money value of any valuable consideration given to the director` GREATER THAN 0)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If in connection with any such transfer the price to be paid to a director ... is in excess of the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of the like shares or any valuable consideration is given to any such director, the excess or the money value of the consideration ... is ... deemed to have been a payment" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))

