-- src:14487 | to any such director, the excess or the money value of the
-- src:14488 | consideration (as the case may be) is for the purposes of this
-- src:14489 | section deemed to have been a payment made to the director by way
-- src:14490 | of compensation for loss of office or as consideration for or in
-- src:14491 | connection with his or her retirement from office.
@ref s 168(4) (src:14478-14491)
GIVEN `the price to be paid to the director for the shares the director holds` IS A NUMBER
      `the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of the like shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the money value of any valuable consideration given to the director` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 168(4) the amount deemed to have been a payment by way of compensation for loss of office` MEANS
    (`s 168(4) the excess of the price paid to the director over the price other holders could have obtained` `the price to be paid to the director for the shares the director holds` `the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of the like shares`) PLUS `the money value of any valuable consideration given to the director`

§ `Section 168(5): payments the references to compensation for loss of office do not include`

-- src:14500 | (a) any payment under an agreement entered into before
-- src:14501 | 1 January 1967;
@ref s 168(5)(a) (src:14500-14501)
GIVEN `the date of the agreement under which the payment is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(5)(a) the payment is made under an agreement entered into before 1 January 1967` MEANS
    IF `the date of the agreement under which the payment is made` LESS THAN Date 1 1 1967
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5) states what any reference "does not include"; a payment under an agreement of 1 January 1967 or later is not named, and the subsection says nothing of it

-- src:14503 | (b) any payment under an agreement particulars of which have
-- src:14504 | been disclosed to and approved by special resolution of the
-- src:14505 | company;
@ref s 168(5)(b) (src:14503-14505)
GIVEN `the payment is made under an agreement particulars of which have been disclosed to and approved by special resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(5)(b) the payment is made under an agreement disclosed to and approved by special resolution of the company` MEANS
    IF `the payment is made under an agreement particulars of which have been disclosed to and approved by special resolution of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5) states what any reference "does not include" and says nothing of any other payment

-- src:14507 | (c) any bona fide payment by way of damages for breach of
-- src:14508 | contract;
@ref s 168(5)(c) (src:14507-14508)
GIVEN `the payment is a bona fide payment by way of damages for breach of contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(5)(c) the payment is a bona fide payment by way of damages for breach of contract` MEANS
    IF `the payment is a bona fide payment by way of damages for breach of contract`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5) states what any reference "does not include" and says nothing of any other payment

-- (d): "where the value or amount of the pension or payment, except insofar as it is attributable to contributions made by the director, does not exceed the total emoluments of the director in the 3 years
-- immediately preceding his or her retirement or death".
-- src:14510 | (d) any bona fide payment by way of pension or lump sum
-- src:14511 | payment in respect of past services, including any
-- src:14512 | superannuation or retiring allowance, superannuation
-- src:14513 | gratuity or similar payment, where the value or amount
-- src:14514 | of the pension or payment, except insofar as it is
-- src:14515 | attributable to contributions made by the director, does
-- src:14516 | not exceed the total emoluments of the director in the
-- src:14517 | 3 years immediately preceding his or her retirement or
-- src:14518 | death; or
@ref s 168(5)(d) (src:14510-14518)
GIVEN `the payment is a bona fide payment by way of pension or lump sum payment in respect of past services, including any superannuation or retiring allowance, superannuation gratuity or similar payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value or amount of the pension or payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of that value or amount attributable to contributions made by the director` IS A NUMBER
      `the total emoluments of the director in the 3 years immediately preceding his or her retirement or death` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(5)(d) the payment is a bona fide pension or lump sum payment in respect of past services within the limit` MEANS
    IF    `the payment is a bona fide payment by way of pension or lump sum payment in respect of past services, including any superannuation or retiring allowance, superannuation gratuity or similar payment`
      AND (`the value or amount of the pension or payment` MINUS `the part of that value or amount attributable to contributions made by the director`) AT MOST `the total emoluments of the director in the 3 years immediately preceding his or her retirement or death`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5) states what any reference "does not include", and "where the value or amount ... does not exceed the total emoluments" limits (d) in its own wording; the subsection says nothing of a payment outside it

-- src:14520 | (e) any payment to a director pursuant to an agreement made
-- src:14521 | between the company and him or her before he or she
-- src:14522 | became a director of the company as the consideration or
-- src:14523 | part of the consideration for the director agreeing to serve
-- src:14524 | the company as a director.
@ref s 168(5)(e) (src:14520-14524)
GIVEN `the payment is made pursuant to an agreement made between the company and the director before the director became a director, as the consideration or part of the consideration for the director agreeing to serve the company as a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(5)(e) the payment is made pursuant to an agreement made before the director became a director` MEANS
    IF `the payment is made pursuant to an agreement made between the company and the director before the director became a director, as the consideration or part of the consideration for the director agreeing to serve the company as a director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5) states what any reference "does not include" and says nothing of any other payment

-- src:14495 | (5) Any reference in this section to payments to any director of a
-- src:14496 | company by way of compensation for loss of office or as
-- src:14497 | consideration for or in connection with his or her retirement from
-- src:14498 | office does not include —
@ref s 168(5) (src:14495-14498)
GIVEN `the answer under paragraph (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under paragraph (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under paragraph (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under paragraph (d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under paragraph (e)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(5) the payment is one that the references in the section to compensation for loss of office do not include` MEANS
    IF    `the answer under paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the answer under paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the answer under paragraph (c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the answer under paragraph (d)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the answer under paragraph (e)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5) lists five kinds of payment that any reference "does not include", with no "only", and says nothing of any other payment

§ `Section 168(6) and (7)`

-- src:14529 | (6) This section is in addition to and not in derogation of any rule of
-- src:14530 | law requiring disclosure to be made with respect to any such
-- src:14531 | payments or any other like payment.
@ref s 168(6) (src:14529-14531)
GIVEN `a rule of law requires disclosure to be made with respect to the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(6) the section displaces a rule of law requiring disclosure to be made with respect to the payment` MEANS
    IF `a rule of law requires disclosure to be made with respect to the payment`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section is in addition to and not in derogation of any rule of law requiring disclosure to be made with respect to any such payments or any other like payment" (a flat negative: N2 of 2026-11-04)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of a rule of law requiring disclosure and says nothing where there is none

-- src:14533 | (7) In this section, “director” includes any person who has at any
-- src:14534 | time been a director of the company or of a corporation which is by
-- src:14535 | virtue of section 6 deemed to be related to the company.
@ref s 168(7) (src:14533-14535)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has at any time been a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has at any time been a director of a corporation that is by virtue of section 6 deemed to be related to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(7) the person is within the word director in the section` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director of the company` OR `the person has at any time been a director of the company` OR `the person has at any time been a director of a corporation that is by virtue of section 6 deemed to be related to the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "In this section, “director” includes any person who has at any time been a director of the company or of a corporation which is by virtue of section 6 deemed to be related to the company" does not say that no other person is a director

§ `Section 169: provision and improvement of a director's emoluments`

DECLARE `s 169 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 169(1) provide or improve emoluments for a director in respect of his or her office as such`

-- (1): "A company must not at any meeting or otherwise provide emoluments or improve emoluments for a director of a company in respect of his or her office as such unless the provision is approved by a resolution
-- that is not related to other matters".
-- src:14539 | 169.—(1) A company must not at any meeting or otherwise provide
-- src:14540 | emoluments or improve emoluments for a director of a company in
-- src:14541 | respect of his or her office as such unless the provision is approved by
-- src:14542 | a resolution that is not related to other matters and any resolution
-- src:14543 | passed in breach of this section is void.
@ref s 169(1) (src:14539-14543)
GIVEN `the company provides emoluments or improves emoluments for a director in respect of his or her office as such` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is approved by a resolution that is not related to other matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169(1) the provision or improvement of the emoluments is barred` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company provides emoluments or improves emoluments for a director in respect of his or her office as such`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "provide emoluments or improve emoluments for a director of a company in respect of his or her office as such" limits the bar in its own wording, and the case falls outside the limit
    ELSE IF `the provision is approved by a resolution that is not related to other matters`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the provision is approved by a resolution that is not related to other matters" (an "unless" once met: fork F-168-1 reading)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:14539 | 169.—(1) A company must not at any meeting or otherwise provide
-- src:14540 | emoluments or improve emoluments for a director of a company in
-- src:14541 | respect of his or her office as such unless the provision is approved by
-- src:14542 | a resolution that is not related to other matters and any resolution
-- src:14543 | passed in breach of this section is void.
@ref s 169(1) (src:14539-14543)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the provision is approved by a resolution that is not related to other matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 169 act`
`s 169(1) the company must not provide or improve a director's emoluments unless approved by a resolution not related to other matters` MEANS
    IF `the provision is approved by a resolution that is not related to other matters`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY Company `the name of the company`
         SHANT `s 169(1) provide or improve emoluments for a director in respect of his or her office as such`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company provided or improved emoluments for a director in respect of his or her office as such without approval by a resolution that is not related to other matters"

-- src:14542 | a resolution that is not related to other matters and any resolution
-- src:14543 | passed in breach of this section is void.
@ref s 169(1) (src:14542-14543)
GIVEN `the resolution was passed in breach of the section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169(1) the resolution is void` MEANS
    IF `the resolution was passed in breach of the section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "any resolution passed in breach of this section is void" speaks only of a resolution passed in breach and says nothing of another

DECLARE `s 169(2) kind of benefit` IS ONE OF
    `s 169(2) fees and percentages`
    `s 169(2) a sum paid by way of expenses allowance`
    `s 169(2) a contribution paid in respect of a director under a pension scheme`
    `s 169(2) a benefit received otherwise than in cash in respect of the director's services as director`
    `s 169(2) some other payment or benefit`

-- src:14545 | (2) In this section, “emoluments” in relation to a director includes
-- src:14546 | fees and percentages, any sums paid by way of expenses allowance
-- src:14547 | insofar as those sums are charged to income tax in Singapore, any
-- src:14548 | contribution paid in respect of a director under any pension scheme
-- src:14549 | and any benefits received by him or her otherwise than in cash in
-- src:14550 | respect of his or her services as director.
@ref s 169(2) (src:14545-14550)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 169(2) kind of benefit`
      `the sum is charged to income tax in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169(2) the payment or benefit is within the word emoluments` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 169(2) some other payment or benefit` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“emoluments” in relation to a director includes fees and percentages, ..." does not say that no other payment is emoluments
    WHEN `s 169(2) a sum paid by way of expenses allowance`
         THEN (IF `the sum is charged to income tax in Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (includes, and limited by its own wording): "any sums paid by way of expenses allowance insofar as those sums are charged to income tax in Singapore" includes such sums to that extent and does not say the rest is not emoluments
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
